 Plasma Cell Disorder", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.03, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Systemic B symptoms are more specific for lymphoid neoplasms, moderately increasing their likelihood while providing minimal impact on myeloid neoplasms."]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.38268576064733106, "posterior": 0.3288872380987961, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["35% blasts in peripheral blood is pathognomonic for leukemia, decisively excluding reactive processes. This provides strong evidence against B1."], "evidence_against": ["Non-specific ataxia alone does not exclude chronic myeloid neoplasms (B5), though the absence of documented MPN history weakens this hypothesis."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.6, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["chronic myeloid leukemia", "polycythemia vera", "essential thrombocythemia", "primary myelofibrosis"]}}, "frontier": ["B3", "B5"], "other_mass": 0.0, "actions_taken": [{"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of 35% blasts in peripheral blood with pancytopenia rule out a non-malignant cause and confirm myeloid neoplasm?", "summary": "35% blasts almost always indicate malignancy, decisively excluding reactive processes. This supports myeloid neoplasms (B2) and lymphoid neoplasms (B3)."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Do the systemic B symptoms and subacute onset strongly support lymphoid neoplasm over myeloid neoplasm?", "summary": "Systemic B symptoms are more specific for lymphoid neoplasms, moderately increasing their likelihood while providing minima